\begin_layout Description
(1) With the 
\series bold
Shell
\series default
 preferences the OS shell can be started within Bio7 with some arguments.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
(2) In the 
\series bold
R
\series default
 preference the R editor script can be executed with the native connection
 instead of the Rserve connection (deprecated - only useful if Rserve is
 started independent from the shell!).
 
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "rnativepreference"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
(3) In the 
\series bold
Python/Blender
\series default
 preference it can be adjusted to execute Python code of the editor with
 a native Python connection instead of the default Jython interpreter.
 The path to a Python interpreter has to be adjusted.
 In addition a Blender Python interpreter (which is embedded in an Blender
 installation) can be used to execute editor code.
 The different options are described in 
\series bold
(4)
\series default
.
 Once again the path has to be adjusted.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Description
(4) In the 
\series bold
Blender Default Options
\series default
 some preferences can be selected and changed to start the Python interpreter
 and execute editor code in different ways.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
None
\series default
 will simply startup Blender without a Python script execution (arguments
 can be specified in the 
\series bold
Blender Arguments
\series default
).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
The option
\series bold
 Interactive Shell
\series default
 if selected starts the Python connection as an interactiv shell (argument:
 --python-console).
 A special script customization is possible by defining code elements which
 will be executed before and after the editor code (the default code in
 the two textfields redraws the 3d GUI of Blender!)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
The option 
\series bold
Python Script 
\series default
starts Blender and executes the editor script in Blender Python without
 an interactive shell.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
With the 
\series bold
Blender Arguments
\series default
 additional arguments can be specified for the startup of Blender (e.g.
 with the option 
\series bold
None
\series default
 some rendering tasks can be executed instead of executing a python script).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Drag, Drop, Compile and Start
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Since Bio7 1.5 it is possible to store grid patterns in an *.xml file.
 If a Java editor is available the source code of an opened editor can be
 saved with the pattern.
 If source in a pattern file is available, too the source of the file will
 be loaded and compiled and the setup method (if available) will be executed.
 This can be used to execute a Java model with drag and drop.
 In addition this drag and drop action can also be used in conjunction with
 different java model types (3d models etc.).
 Please note that a package declaration in a Java file is not supported!
 Simply use the default /src project folder as created by the Bio7 project
 wizard when saving the file.
 Some examples can be found on GitHub: 
\begin_inset Flex URL
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

https://github.com/Bio7/Bio7
\end_layout

\end_inset

 
\end_layout

